 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of voxels in the chunk ($WIDTH \times HEIGHT \times DEPTH$) [S9, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(F)$ where $F$ is the number of visible faces. The packed vertex format uses 8 bytes per vertex [S7, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Reduces draw calls significantly by batching faces into a single mesh per chunk [S2, unofficial]. Scales better than instancing for large numbers of blocks [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Modifying a single block requires regenerating the entire chunk mesh, which is computationally expensive [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Dynamic Updates:** Can be optimized by only rebuilding chunks near the player or within a configurable distance [S9, unofficial].
